      "title": "DendROS - colored ROS2 terminal output with utils",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/dendros-colored-ros2-terminal-output-with-utils/58797",
      "summary": "Hi all, I’d like to share DendROS , an open-source tool that makes ROS 2 terminal output easier to read. When a launch file starts thirty nodes, they all print to the same terminal in the same color, and the line you need has usually scrolled away by the time you look for it. DendROS gives each group of nodes its own color and opens ros2 launch in a viewer where you can scroll, search and filter the log while the launch keeps running. Code (MIT): GitHub - mlisi1/DendROS: Color-coded terminal output for ROS 2 — group nodes by color, highlight crashes and tracebacks, zero changes to your launch files or workflow. · GitHub Docs: DendROS How it works DendROS wraps the ros2 command with a bash function and pipes the output of ros2 launch and ros2 run through a colorizer. You describe your groups in a dendROS.yaml file inside your package: groups: localization: color: \"bold blue\" label: \"LOC\" nodes: - slam_toolbox - amcl navigation: color: \"green\" label: \"NAV\" nodes: - nav2_* There are no changes to launch files and no dependencies beyond PyYAML. A package without a config is passed through untouched, exit codes are preserved, and shell completion for ros2 keeps working. What it does Col",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-12T16:21:54+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-12T16:21:54+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "DendROS - colored ROS2 terminal output with utils - Projects - Open Robotics Discourse DendROS - colored ROS2 terminal output with utils Projects ros2 , terminal , cli , tools mlisi1 October 12, 2026, 4:21pm 1 Hi all, I’d like to share DendROS , an open-source tool that makes ROS 2 terminal output easier to read. When a launch file starts thirty nodes, they all print to the same terminal in the same color, and the line you need has usually scrolled away by the time you look for it. DendROS gives each group of nodes its own color and opens ros2 launch in a viewer where you can scroll, search and filter the log while the launch keeps running. Code (MIT): GitHub - mlisi1/DendROS: Color-coded terminal output for ROS 2 — group nodes by color, highlight crashes and tracebacks, zero changes to your launch files or workflow. · GitHub Docs: DendROS How it works DendROS wraps the ros2 command with a bash function and pipes the output of ros2 launch and ros2 run through a colorizer. You describe your groups in a dendROS.yaml file inside your package: groups: localization: color: \"bold blue\" label: \"LOC\" nodes: - slam_toolbox - amcl navigation: color: \"green\" label: \"NAV\" nodes: - nav2_* There are no changes to launch files and no dependencies beyond PyYAML. A package without a config is passed through untouched, exit codes are preserved, and shell completion for ros2 keeps working. What it does Colors and badges per group. Each group gets a color and an optional badge such as [LOC] . Node names accept wildcards, and you can highlight keywords per group or for the whole package. Group colors, badges and keyword highlighting 1096×562 117 KB A viewer for ros2 launch . The log stays in a scrollback buffer, long lines are wrapped, and you can select text with the mouse to copy it. Press \\ to open a console with these commands: Command What it does focus <node>... Show only some nodes. It matches the process name or the logger name, so components in a container can be picked one by one level <lvl> Show lines at a severity or worse. Tracebacks always stay visible grep <text> Live text filter with the matches highlighted find <text> Search the scrollback. Tab and Shift+Tab step through the matches mute / unmute Hide and restore noisy nodes mark [label] Insert a timestamped separator line tee <file> Save the lines currently shown to a file Filters combine and Esc removes the most recent one. The same commands work from another terminal (dendros focus planner_server , dendros grep timeout ), which helps when the launch runs in another tmux pane. dendros reopen brings back the last run after it has ended. The viewer steps aside when the output is piped or redirected, so scripts and CI see plain output. If you prefer the normal scrolling output, set launch_mode: classic . Crashes, tracebacks and parameter changes. A banner shows which node died and its exit code. Python tracebacks are highlighted. When a parameter changes at runtime, a notice shows the node, the parameter and the old and new value. The ros2 CLI in the same colors. ros2 node list , node info , topic list , service list , action list , param list and param describe use the group colors of the running launch. Topics are colored by their publisher and show publisher and subscriber counts. ros2 topic list colored by publisher group 1096×247 20.7 KB Setup helpers. dendros init scans your launch files and writes a first config. dendros config is a small terminal UI for the global settings. dendros disable and dendros enable switch the tool off and on in every terminal, including for launches that are already running. Install git clone https://github.com/mlisi1/DendROS cd DendROS && bash install.sh && source ~/.bashrc Then, from the root of your bringup package: dendros init # writes config/dendROS.yaml from your launch files colcon build --packages-select my_bringup ros2 launch my_bringup main.launch.py It is plain Python 3 and bash, and it runs on the host or in Docker. The shell integration is bash only for now. I develop and test it on Jazzy; nothing in it is specific to one distribution. Feedback I’d like to hear how it behaves on your setup, especially: terminals where the viewer looks wrong or the mouse copy does not reach the clipboard launch output that is not matched or colored as you would expect console commands or CLI subcommands you find yourself missing Issues are welcome on GitHub . peci1 October 12, 2026, 5:22pm 2 Please, take at least the minimal effort to correctly format the LLM output. 1 Like mlisi1 October 12, 2026, 7:21pm 3 While the post was indeed generated by Claude (and then overseen by me), I honestly thought the Markdown would have been rendered the same as the VS Code extension I use. My mistake, I will fix it as soon as I can. 1 Like Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity Ros2_info — a terminal workspace lens for ROS 2 (TUI + optional local AI) ROS General release , ros2 , cli , ros 4 296 July 15, 2026 Better Console Logging ROS General ros2 , logging 21 2008 January 27, 2026 ROS 2 launch GUI Projects ros2 , launch 9 2165 August 26, 2025 🤖 ROS 2 Info v2.0.0 is out — fastfetch for your ROS 2 workspace Projects release , ros2 , terminal , ros 0 135 May 11, 2026 Tf_tree_terminal Projects ros2 , tf2 12 1038 January 12, 2026",
