      "articleText": "Robotics News Humanoid Robots Video Friday: Robot Decommissioning Takes a Fun Turn Your weekly selection of awesome robot videos Evan Ackerman 09 Oct 2026 2 min read Evan Ackerman is IEEE Spectrum’s robotics editor. Even if it's AI, does a ball pit make decommissioning fun for the robot—or only for those watching? AI generated by Devanthro Video Friday is your weekly selection of awesome robotics videos, collected by your friends at IEEE Spectrum robotics. We also post a weekly calendar of upcoming robotics events for the next few months. Please send us your events for inclusion. CoRL 2026 : 9–12 November 2026, AUSTIN Humanoids 2026 : 6–9 December 2026, SANTA CLARA, CA Enjoy today’s videos! It’s possible that I wasn’t the only one who thought that Figure’s recent stunt was somewhat ridiculous. Devanthro is in fact selling these plastic balls for $1000 each, and they’ll arrive in time for Christmas. [ Devanthro ] Not that anyone uses ringtones anymore, but if we did, this would be absolutely everywhere and I’d be loving it. [ Pollen ] Let’s not get too excited, but this thread-like linear motor is pretty sweet. [ Ecole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne LMTS ] What is this robot for? It’s for doing exactly what you see here, that’s what it’s for. [ RAI Institute ] Humanoid robots still struggle to plan contact-rich whole-body manipulation from egocentric RGB and proprioception . Workhorse learns such manipulation from robot-free human demonstrations. On a real Unitree G1, Workhorse sorts boxes with its hands and a kick, catches a thrown box, and topples and climbs a suitcase. Yeah that happens to me too when I have a communication failure. [ Hybrid Robotics ] A car wash that models your vehicle then cleans it with robot arms ? Interesting idea. The recent reviews from this location suggest that the robots aren’t quite up to snuff yet, but really seems like there’s potential here. [ KUKA ] So this is not the worst idea I’ve ever seen for what to do with humanoid robots. [ DEEP Robotics ] Some lovely manipulation with a deceptively simple gripper . [ Generalist ] I am genuinely embarrassed to say that this robot dances better than I do. [ General Robotics Lab ] MIT researchers developed SANDO, a new navigation system that helps robots safely navigate unfamiliar environments while avoiding moving obstacles. The system can rapidly plan and adjust a collision-free path using onboard sensors and computing, with safety backed by mathematical guarantees. [ MIT News ] Can you spot the part of this video that I’m side eyeing? Yep, it’s where the middle clip starts after the hand already has a good grip on that peelable strip. [ Sanctuary AI ] Inspired by feather stars, the NC State researchers report a soft underwater swimming robot capable of achieving three distinct swimming modes—jellyfish-like vertical swimming, fish-like directional steering, and rotor-like 3D reorientation—using only two pneumatic inputs. [ NC State University ] Here’s a series of mini-keynotes from ICRA earlier this year, on manipulation, humaonids, and embodied design. [ ICRA 2026 ] From Your Site Articles Video Friday: Reachy 2 › Video Friday: Reachy Mini Brings the Cute › Related Articles Around the Web Reachy Mini, amazing to build with the kid, painful ... › Reachy Mini - Open source expressive companion robot | Pollen Robotics › Video Friday robotics videos humanoid robots robot arms industrial robotics robot grippers Evan Ackerman Evan Ackerman is a senior editor at IEEE Spectrum . Since 2007, he has written over 6,000 articles on robotics and technology. He has a degree in Martian geology and is excellent at playing bagpipes. Aerospace News NASA Wants More Than 70 Moon Landings in the Next Decade—But How? 10h 5 min read AI Energy Sponsored Article Computing The Future Is Fanless: 100% Heat Capture for Liquid Cooled AI Servers 22 Sep 2026 3 min read Energy News First Utility-Scale Enhanced Geothermal Plant Goes Live 12h 3 min read Robo