      "summary": "Hi everyone! I’ve been building RobotLens , a native robotics engineering workspace that brings visualization, debugging, diagnostics, simulation, and development workflows into one connected environment. My background is in computer graphics and game development. When I started learning ROS 2, I found myself constantly switching between terminals, visualizers, logs, simulators, and other tools. Each tool was useful on its own, but as a beginner, I often struggled to understand how everything connected and what was actually happening across the system. That experience led me to start building RobotLens. Coming from graphics and game development, I’ve always appreciated how tools like Unity and Unreal bring complex workflows into a single, interactive workspace. I wanted to explore a similar approach for robotics engineering. Here’s what’s been built so far: ROS 2 or Zenoh Workspace: Live discovery, topic inspection, TF visualization, diagnostics, and communication backend support. Visualization: Native Vulkan rendering, robot visualization, and interactive scene manipulation, topic visualization. Simulation: Gazebo and MuJoCo integration, with support for different simulation workf",
