      "title": "Redesigning source control at Anthropic",
      "link": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/13/redesigning-source-control-at-anthropic/",
      "summary": "Redesigning source control at Anthropic Interesting piece from Anthropic describing why and how they built their own custom alternative to Git, based on the dramatic increase in rate of changes to their code after the past six months. In May 2026, Anthropic averaged around 2,500 code changes merged per day; as of September, we merged over 30,000 per day. They included a chart showing those changes. I had Claude modify their chart (code here ) to add markers for the public releases of each of their models in 2026: This shows public release dates, not the date when models became available for Anthropic's internal use. My guess is that the introduction of Fable/Mythos class models is a key factor in the increased coding velocity. \"Antique\" is their new code review system. The source control system is called Scion, and sounds to me like a reinvention of centralized source control along the lines of Subversion. They had some pretty extreme requirements: The history of our main branch alone is almost 100 GB, and a compressed working copy is over 25 GB. We perform on the order of 25 million code checkouts per day for CI, before counting developer environments, agent sandboxes, and researc",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-13T23:00:06+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-13T23:00:06+00:00",
      "source": "Simon Willison",
      "section_hint": "AI",
      "articleText": "Redesigning source control at Anthropic Simon Willison’s Weblog Newsletter Sponsored by: Pomerium — Static OAuth scopes won't stop AI agent breakouts. Upgrade to Pomerium's agentic access management trusted by NVIDIA and OpenAI 13th October 2026 - Link Blog Redesigning source control at Anthropic (via ) Interesting piece from Anthropic describing why and how they built their own custom alternative to Git, based on the dramatic increase in rate of changes to their code after the past six months. In May 2026, Anthropic averaged around 2,500 code changes merged per day; as of September, we merged over 30,000 per day. They included a chart showing those changes. I had Claude modify their chart (code here ) to add markers for the public releases of each of their models in 2026: This shows public release dates, not the date when models became available for Anthropic's internal use. My guess is that the introduction of Fable/Mythos class models is a key factor in the increased coding velocity. \"Antique\" is their new code review system. The source control system is called Scion, and sounds to me like a reinvention of centralized source control along the lines of Subversion. They had some pretty extreme requirements: The history of our main branch alone is almost 100 GB, and a compressed working copy is over 25 GB. We perform on the order of 25 million code checkouts per day for CI, before counting developer environments, agent sandboxes, and research jobs. Fetched naively, that would be over 600 PB of git traffic per day. The new system was built by a team of seven people, and the migration from Git was completed in five months. As an aside, I've been trying adversarial review in my own projects recently, where you have a model try and find flaws (I often play Claude and GPT off against each other). This note from the article reflected my own experience with that: Anthropic also makes extensive use of adversarial review, and, while this is incredibly effective in many ways, it can also be myopic, so skilled engineers needed to steer Claude away from over-engineering parts of the system in response to hypothetical concerns. Posted 13th October 2026 at 11 pm Recent articles Hello Python 3.15, goodbye 3.10, and now I can use 3.11 - 12th October 2026 A new feature for my blog, built using my voice - 9th October 2026 Claude Haiku 5.5 - 7th October 2026 We're going to need default hard budget caps on pretty much everything - 3rd October 2026 This is a link post by Simon Willison, posted on 13th October 2026 . git 58 migrations 15 version-control 13 ai 2,279 generative-ai 2,021 llms 1,987 anthropic 348 agentic-engineering 66 Monthly briefing Sponsor me for $10/month and get a curated email digest of the month's most important LLM developments. Pay me to send you less! Sponsor & subscribe Disclosures Colophon © 2002 2003 2004 2005 2006 2007 2008 2009 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015 2016 2017 2018 2019 2020 2021 2022 2023 2024 2025 2026",
