      "title": "NYSOFA expands partnership with Intuition Robotics to bring ElliQ to more seniors",
      "link": "https://www.therobotreport.com/nysofa-expands-partnership-intuition-robotics-bring-elliq-more-seniors/",
      "summary": "With the expansion, NYSOFA and Intuition Robotics established a new three-year, $2.1 million agreement to keep rolling out ElliQ. The post NYSOFA expands partnership with Intuition Robotics to bring ElliQ to more seniors appeared first on The Robot Report .",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-13T23:22:05+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-13T23:22:05+00:00",
      "source": "The Robot Report",
      "section_hint": "트렌드",
      "articleText": "ElliQ extracts memories from every conversation with the user and classifies them based on importance and relevance, injecting context into future conversations. | Source: Intuition Robotics The New York State Office for the Aging, or NYSOFA, last week extended its partnership with Intuition Robotics. The company will continue bringing its ElliQ AI companion to aging New Yorkers at risk of loneliness and social isolation. With the expansion, NYSOFA and Intuition Robotics created a new three-year, $2.1 million agreement. The expansion builds on the organizations’ three years of experience working together. During that time, ElliQ has demonstrated its ability to reduce loneliness and improve health and wellbeing. The robot also helps older adults remain healthier and more independent in their own homes. “Loneliness and isolation are commonly heard today, but make no mistake, the health effects are devastating, and NYSOFA is working continuously to provide the help older New Yorkers need,” said Greg Olsen, director of the office . “ElliQ is an essential tool to help combat the loneliness epidemic, joining dozens of other projects launched by NYSOFA to overcome the digital divide, address social isolation, improve health and wellness, and support caregivers.” NYSOFA established its first public-private partnership in 2018, following a report by AARP and the U.S. Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) on the impact of loneliness and social isolation on older adults and Medicare spending. It stated that loneliness and isolation are equivalent to smoking almost a pack of cigarettes per day, cost Medicare more than $7 billion to treat, and make chronic conditions worse. They can also increase mortality, depression and anxiety, and the risk of dementia. In addition to its partnership with NYSOFA, Intuition Robotics has similar partnerships in Wisconsin, Florida, and Washington. In Washington, the program is aimed at Medicaid recipients . The Ramat Gan, Israel-based company was founded in 2016. NYSOFA reports favorable results with ElliQ so far Since launching in 2022, hundreds of older adults across New York have received ElliQ through the program, while demand continues to grow. More than 3,500 older adults applied to participate in 2025 alone. “Perhaps most importantly, the partnership has reinforced that effective AI companionship isn’t just about answering questions or providing reminders. It’s about proactively engaging older adults, understanding their individual needs, and building the trust and familiarity that make technology a meaningful part of their everyday lives,” an Intuition Robotics spokesperson told The Robot Report . Newly reported program data from 2026 demonstrates ElliQ’s impact on the older adults living with the device: 92% of ElliQ users find the companion useful. Participants engage with ElliQ an average of 48 times per day, up from 29 daily interactions in reporting from previous years. 94% report feeling less lonely, 97% report improved overall wellbeing, 88% say ElliQ has made a positive difference in their daily lives, and 79% feel more connected to the world around them. Every month, 88% of participants engage in two-way conversations with ElliQ, 92% regularly share updates about their wellbeing, and 81% participate in physical activity encouraged by ElliQ. 88% of users find that ElliQ has both improved their life for the better and their quality of life. “This partnership extension continues our long term partnership with the state of New York, and its Office for the Aging, reflecting three years of measurable, record-breaking engagement results: older adults across New York are engaging with ElliQ more often, feeling less lonely, and staying more connected to the people who matter to them,” said Dor Skuler, co-founder and CEO of Intuition Robotics. “What we have seen is that an AI companion who remembers the older adult, checks in every morning, and encourages them to take a walk or call their daughter can meaningfully change how connected and independent someone feels,” he added. “That is the outcome New York continues to invest in.” Register now and help us celebrate 20 years of RoboBusiness! About The Author Brianna Wessling Brianna Wessling is an Associate Editor, Robotics, WTWH Media. She joined WTWH Media in November 2021, after graduating from the University of Kansas with degrees in Journalism and English. She covers a wide range of robotics topics, but specializes in women in robotics, robotics in healthcare, and space robotics. She can be reached at [email protected] Tell Us What You Think! Cancel reply This site uses Akismet to reduce spam. Learn how your comment data is processed. Related Articles Read More > Hello Robot, A&K Robotics to discuss how robots navigate crowded indoor spaces at RoboBusiness Promise Robotics partners with D.R. Horton on physical AI for homebuilding Will ‘boring’ robots win in the real world? Why robotic form should follow workflow Why dexterity is physical AI’s real bottleneck",
