      "title": "Hello Robot, A&K Robotics to discuss how robots navigate crowded indoor spaces at RoboBusiness",
      "link": "https://www.therobotreport.com/hello-robot-ak-robotics-discuss-how-robots-navigate-crowded-indoor-spaces-robobusiness/",
      "summary": "As robots move beyond warehouses and other controlled environments and into everyday life, navigation challenges will be critical. The post Hello Robot, A&K Robotics to discuss how robots navigate crowded indoor spaces at RoboBusiness appeared first on The Robot Report .",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-13T19:48:58+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-13T19:48:58+00:00",
      "source": "The Robot Report",
      "section_hint": "트렌드",
      "articleText": "On the left, Hello Robot’s Stretch 4, and on the right, A&K Robotics’ Cruz autonomous pod. | Source: Hello Robot, A&K Robotics Consumer-facing spaces are dynamic, crowded, and highly unpredictable, requiring robots to safely navigate around constantly changing obstacles, operate in diverse lighting conditions, navigate narrow passages and cluttered spaces, integrate with existing infrastructure, and balance autonomy with safety. As robots move beyond warehouses and other controlled environments and into everyday life, solving these navigation challenges will be critical to achieving broad consumer acceptance and large-scale deployment. At RoboBusiness 2026, Aaron Edsinger, the co-founder and CEO of Hello Robot , and Matt Anderson, the co-founder and CEO of A&K Robotics , will take part in the session, “Shared Spaces: Navigating Challenges for Indoor Robots.” RoboBusiness will be on Oct. 20 and 21 in Santa Clara, Calif. Edsinger and Anderson will give their talk at 3:30 p.m. PT on the first day of the show in the Engineering Theater. Meet the speakers Aaron Edsinger is co-founder and CEO of Hello Robot, which developing practical, safe, and accessible robots for people. With a passion for building robots and robot companies, he has founded four companies focused on bringing human collaborative robots to the consumer, manufacturing, healthcare and research markets. Two of these companies, Meka Robotics and Redwood Robotics, were acquired by Google in 2013. As robotics director at Google, Edsinger led the business, product and technical development of two of Google’s central investments in robotics, and worked closely with senior vice president and C-level executives to define the overall robotics strategy. Edsinger is a recognized robotics innovator with a broad understanding of the entire robot product design stack, including human–robot interaction, UX design, and mechanical design. He is also an expert in design for manufacture, industrial design, software architecture, and real-time control, as well as design of force-controlled arms, actuators, hands and humanoids. Matt Anderson is co-founder and CEO of A&K Robotics, which is building autonomous mobility infrastructure for complex, human-centered environments such as airports. He leads the company’s product strategy, which includes Cruz, a self-driving mobility robot that carries passengers through high-traffic, dynamic environments such as airport terminals, and Kineos AI, a platform for socially intelligent autonomy that enables systems to move naturally through dynamic spaces. Anderson brings credibility with enterprise and public-sector partners by translating advanced autonomy into institution-ready solutions. He has over 10 years of experience building and bringing to market advanced technologies ranging from autonomous aerial drones to surgical devices. Matt is an alumnus of Creative Destruction Lab’s AI and Machine Learning program. In a past life, he was a Chartered Accountant working in finance, investment, and business development. Register now for RoboBusiness RoboBusiness 2026 is the leading event for commercial robotics developers. Attendees can gain the latest insights from experts in robotics and AI on cutting-edge research; industry trends; and innovative applications in sectors such as manufacturing, healthcare, agriculture, logistics, and more. The show also features a number of networking opportunities to give attendees a chance to connect with other experts in the industry. Buy your full conference pass and gain full access to all keynotes, technical sessions, networking receptions, and special events. Discounts are also available for academia, associations, and corporate groups. Please email events[at]arrowfly.com for more details about our discount programs. For information about sponsorship and exhibition opportunities, download the prospectus . Questions regarding sponsorship opportunities should be directed to Colleen Sepich at csepich[AT]arrowfly.com. Tell Us What You Think! Cancel reply This site uses Akismet to reduce spam. Learn how your comment data is processed. Related Articles Read More > Groceryshop 2026 shows that retail robots are ready to scale, use AI Harmonic Drive to share how integrated actuators can reduce engineering at RoboBusiness Eli Lilly, Purdue to share field learnings on human robot interaction at RoboBusiness The Robot Report parent Arrowfly launches AI for Engineers platform, events for engineers navigating AI",
