      "title": "These weeks at Open Robotics HQ (since pre-ROSCon Global)",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/these-weeks-at-open-robotics-hq-since-pre-roscon-global/58845",
      "summary": "Did I say I’d publish one of these right after ROSCon Global? I was overly ambitious (so, so overly ambitious). Truth be told, Open Robotics HQ is still digging out from all the good stuff that happened in Toronto. There’s a whole lot involved with tying off an event, not least of which are the dozens of follow-up conversations that started while in Toronto. We’re closing the loop on a lot of community questions, including how you can help and contribute more to our work, what it would look like if you joined the OSRA, how we can help you better engage with the community, how you can organize a local event, and more. ROSCon Global always happens right around the transition between Q3 and Q4 for the year. This means that aside from tying off matters from the event we also need to close out a quarter and prep for the next one. Q4 is always special (read: hectic!), because it includes working to wrap up one year while also setting the scene for another successful year to follow. Which is to say, there’s an awful lot of planning, organizing, and prioritizing happening and that takes way more time than you’d expect. There is also a bunch of local ROSCons coming up; there are six of them",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-14T04:24:52+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-14T04:24:52+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "These weeks at Open Robotics HQ (since pre-ROSCon Global) - Community News - Open Robotics Discourse These weeks at Open Robotics HQ (since pre-ROSCon Global) Community News weekly-update vmb October 14, 2026, 4:24am 1 Did I say I’d publish one of these right after ROSCon Global? I was overly ambitious (so, so overly ambitious). Truth be told, Open Robotics HQ is still digging out from all the good stuff that happened in Toronto. There’s a whole lot involved with tying off an event, not least of which are the dozens of follow-up conversations that started while in Toronto. We’re closing the loop on a lot of community questions, including how you can help and contribute more to our work, what it would look like if you joined the OSRA, how we can help you better engage with the community, how you can organize a local event, and more. ROSCon Global always happens right around the transition between Q3 and Q4 for the year. This means that aside from tying off matters from the event we also need to close out a quarter and prep for the next one. Q4 is always special (read: hectic!), because it includes working to wrap up one year while also setting the scene for another successful year to follow. Which is to say, there’s an awful lot of planning, organizing, and prioritizing happening and that takes way more time than you’d expect. There is also a bunch of local ROSCons coming up; there are six of them just in the last three months of the year. The local teams do most of the heavy lifting (thank you!), but it all still requires a lot of coordination here in HQ. Of course, the plans we made earlier in the year are still moving forward, so we’re fitting those tasks in there. We’re working on building partnerships with other open source organizations, and investigating how we can work with some academic institutions. There’s also the standing TGC meeting coming up next week, which always requires a lot of preparation. We have some really good stuff on the agenda, though, so keep an eye out for those meeting minutes! And, naturally, the yearly audit continues its crawl toward completion. Still. This may all sound a bit vague, but that’s a necessary evil. If I listed out everything that’s happened since before ROSCon Global y’all could just read this post to your kids to get them to sleep instead of singing a lullaby. There’s been so much going on and it’s been a while since the last update, so you get a summary rather than details. These have been the highlights from the past few weeks at Open Robotics HQ. 2 Likes Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity This Fortnight at Open Robotics Headquarters (2026-08-24) Community News 0 126 September 9, 2026 This Week at Open Robotics Headquarters (2026-08-03) Community News weekly-update 0 152 August 11, 2026 This Week at Open Robotics Headquarters (2026-08-10) Community News weekly-update 0 150 August 18, 2026 This Week at Open Robotics Headquarters (2026-07-27) Community News weekly-update 0 170 August 4, 2026 This Week at Open Robotics Headquarters (2026-08-17) Community News weekly-update 0 195 August 25, 2026",
      "articleUrl": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/these-weeks-at-open-robotics-hq-since-pre-roscon-global/58845",
      "articleFetchedAt": "2026-10-14T23:31:27.635943+00:00",
      "articleStatus": "fetched",
      "date": "2026-10-15"
    },
