      "title": "Ros2_pulse: topic rates on a Grafana dashboard, now counting rclpy nodes and loaned messages",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros2-pulse-topic-rates-on-a-grafana-dashboard-now-counting-rclpy-nodes-and-loaned-messages/58863",
      "summary": "Some updates on ros2_pulse since the first post (Ros2_pulse: per-topic rates and node liveness, including intra-process, on stock binaries ), the LD_PRELOAD probe that counts per-topic rates and node liveness from the tracetools hooks instead of subscribing. Python nodes are counted on both sides now. Before, a Python subscriber’s deliveries never showed up, because rclpy isn’t instrumented. The probe now also hooks the rmw_take tracepoint, so rclpy (and rclc) receives count too. rclcpp still counts at callback_start , so nothing is counted twice. Needs Cyclone or Fast DDS, or Connext from Jazzy. Loaned messages. At the tracepoint level a loan looks like a normal publish, or on Humble like nothing at all. The probe now wraps rcl_publish_loaned_message / rcl_take_loaned_message and prints a separate loaned rate per topic. Worth knowing: from Jazzy, Fast DDS loans any plain type by default, so a Float64 publisher may be going through loans without you asking. Came out of a question by @armaho on rclcpp#3153. Grafana. pulse-export serves the probe’s windows as Prometheus metrics on :9464 and can push OTLP/HTTP. The screenshot above is a live run on my laptop, one camera topic drops un",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-14T16:34:03+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-14T16:34:03+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "Ros2_pulse: topic rates on a Grafana dashboard, now counting rclpy nodes and loaned messages - Projects - Open Robotics Discourse Ros2_pulse: topic rates on a Grafana dashboard, now counting rclpy nodes and loaned messages Projects ros2 , tracing , humble , jazzy , kilted TanayK07 October 14, 2026, 4:34pm 1 ros2_pulse Grafana dashboard 2400×1500 343 KB Some updates on ros2_pulse since the first post (Ros2_pulse: per-topic rates and node liveness, including intra-process, on stock binaries ), the LD_PRELOAD probe that counts per-topic rates and node liveness from the tracetools hooks instead of subscribing. Python nodes are counted on both sides now. Before, a Python subscriber’s deliveries never showed up, because rclpy isn’t instrumented. The probe now also hooks the rmw_take tracepoint, so rclpy (and rclc) receives count too. rclcpp still counts at callback_start , so nothing is counted twice. Needs Cyclone or Fast DDS, or Connext from Jazzy. Loaned messages. At the tracepoint level a loan looks like a normal publish, or on Humble like nothing at all. The probe now wraps rcl_publish_loaned_message / rcl_take_loaned_message and prints a separate loaned rate per topic. Worth knowing: from Jazzy, Fast DDS loans any plain type by default, so a Float64 publisher may be going through loans without you asking. Came out of a question by @armaho on rclcpp#3153. Grafana. pulse-export serves the probe’s windows as Prometheus metrics on :9464 and can push OTLP/HTTP. The screenshot above is a live run on my laptop, one camera topic drops under its 25 Hz floor and the warn lights up. Docker compose with Prometheus, Grafana and the dashboard: ros2_pulse/examples/grafana at main · TanayK07/ros2_pulse · GitHub Smaller things. The startup banner prints the tracetools version and warns on one CI doesn’t run (thanks @christophebedard for the stability answer). pulse-top reads the default text log and has --theme light , thanks to @peci1 trying it on Kilted. A process frozen with SIGSTOP now shows the real gap after it resumes. 30 s explainer on why ros2 topic hz costs CPU on intra-process topics: https://youtu.be/YH8w2bI2EjM Install: sudo apt install ros-$ROS_DISTRO-ros2-pulse (Humble, Jazzy, Kilted). The rclpy and loan counting are in 0.6.0, which reaches apt with the next sync, until then build from main. Code: GitHub - TanayK07/ros2_pulse: Near-zero-overhead ROS 2 topic/node frequency probe (inter + intra process) via an LD_PRELOAD tracetools shim. · GitHub Feedback welcome, especially if it breaks on your setup. 1 Like Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity Ros2_pulse: per-topic rates and node liveness, including intra-process, on stock binaries Projects ros2 , tracing , humble , jazzy , kilted 14 469 October 14, 2026 How do you monitor your robot diagnostics (topic rates)? ROS General ros2 25 2830 January 10, 2025 ROSscope Open source observability platform for ROS 2 fleets (v0.1.0) Projects release , ros2 , ros , humble 0 198 June 7, 2026 Project Proposal:ros2 tool to collect topic metrics Projects 7 2521 August 15, 2023 New tool: ros2sysmon - monitor nodes, topics, ifs, and more in one utility ROS General ros2 9 1217 September 18, 2025",
      "articleUrl": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros2-pulse-topic-rates-on-a-grafana-dashboard-now-counting-rclpy-nodes-and-loaned-messages/58863",
      "articleFetchedAt": "2026-10-14T23:31:27.644188+00:00",
      "articleStatus": "fetched",
      "date": "2026-10-15"
