      "title": "AI-assisted inspection of ROS 2 systems: a preview of DDS Monitor Pro’s MCP integration",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ai-assisted-inspection-of-ros-2-systems-a-preview-of-dds-monitor-pro-s-mcp-integration/58853",
      "summary": "Hi everyone, We at eProsima are sharing a preview of the upcoming AI capabilities in DDS Monitor Pro, with a workflow that is also relevant to engineers working with DDS-based ROS 2 systems. The Monitor’s built-in Model Context Protocol (MCP) server connects an MCP-compatible AI assistant to the system information and operations available in the Monitor. You can ask questions about the running system and inspect the resulting entities, charts and operations in the workspace. The preview demonstrates four workflows: Explore discovered applications, topics, publishers and subscribers. Create graphs from selected topic fields. Investigate a communication problem using endpoint configuration, including a reliability QoS mismatch. Publish sample data to a selected topic in a test environment and observe the response. For ROS 2 deployments using DDS, the connection is the underlying DDS topics and endpoints. The Monitor works at that layer; this is not a claim that it understands every ROS graph concept or supports every ROS middleware implementation. Fast DDS Pro can also be integrated into ROS 2 and Vulcanexus to provide additional communication capabilities and professional tools. Tha",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-14T09:09:24+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-14T09:09:24+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "AI-assisted inspection of ROS 2 systems: a preview of DDS Monitor Pro’s MCP integration - ROS General - Open Robotics Discourse AI-assisted inspection of ROS 2 systems: a preview of DDS Monitor Pro’s MCP integration ROS ROS General ros2 , fastdds Jaime_Martin_Losa October 14, 2026, 9:09am 1 Hi everyone, We at eProsima are sharing a preview of the upcoming AI capabilities in DDS Monitor Pro, with a workflow that is also relevant to engineers working with DDS-based ROS 2 systems. The Monitor’s built-in Model Context Protocol (MCP) server connects an MCP-compatible AI assistant to the system information and operations available in the Monitor. You can ask questions about the running system and inspect the resulting entities, charts and operations in the workspace. The preview demonstrates four workflows: Explore discovered applications, topics, publishers and subscribers. Create graphs from selected topic fields. Investigate a communication problem using endpoint configuration, including a reliability QoS mismatch. Publish sample data to a selected topic in a test environment and observe the response. For ROS 2 deployments using DDS, the connection is the underlying DDS topics and endpoints. The Monitor works at that layer; this is not a claim that it understands every ROS graph concept or supports every ROS middleware implementation. Fast DDS Pro can also be integrated into ROS 2 and Vulcanexus to provide additional communication capabilities and professional tools. That integration is distinct from the requirements for inspecting a particular system with the Monitor. The linked videos demonstrate the DDS workflows. For a specific ROS 2 setup, compatibility and the available operations depend on the middleware, versions, topic type information and configuration. DDS Monitor Pro is a commercial product. These new capabilities are in final testing, with release expected in the coming weeks. The MCP server starts disabled. Once enabled, connected clients can invoke supported operations without a separate approval prompt for each action, so use trusted clients and a test environment for publishing data. Watch the announcement: Explore the preview, short demonstrations and tutorial: https://www.eprosima.com/middleware/tools/dds-monitor-pro/ai-preview Which ROS 2 inspection or debugging tasks would you find most useful to perform through this interface? We would welcome examples of your workflows and questions about compatibility. Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity Introducing CycloneDDS Insight - Graphical DDS Inspection and Debugging for ROS 2 ROS General ros2 , dds 0 234 June 20, 2026 DDS Monitoring for ROS2 - ROS Developers OpenClass #187 Training & Education ros2 , dds 2 1843 May 11, 2024 How to track DDS performance in ROS 2 ROS General ros2 , dds , fastdds 1 1851 October 29, 2021 Amazing ROS 2 MCP: Native ROS 2 MCP server for AI-assisted robotics agents Projects ros2 , ai , mcp 0 286 June 4, 2026 How do you monitor your robot diagnostics (topic rates)? ROS General ros2 25 2830 January 10, 2025",
      "articleUrl": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ai-assisted-inspection-of-ros-2-systems-a-preview-of-dds-monitor-pro-s-mcp-integration/58853",
      "articleFetchedAt": "2026-10-14T23:31:27.650641+00:00",
      "articleStatus": "fetched",
      "date": "2026-10-15"
    },
